    "q-279986": {
      "dom_id": "step-q279986",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x=1$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ If the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ are written in **ascending order**, what are their values? Express your answers in terms of $\\pi .$\n\n${x}_{1}=${{field-1}}$,\\,$\n${x}_{2}=${{field-2}}$,\\,$\n${x}_{3}=${{field-3}}$,\\,$\n${x}_{4}=${{field-4}}",
      "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{8}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{9\\pi }{8}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x=\\frac{13\\pi }{8}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{8},\\frac{5\\pi }{8},\\frac{9\\pi }{8},\\frac{13\\pi }{8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{8},\\,{x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{8},\\,{x}_{3}=\\frac{9\\pi }{8},\\,{x}_{4}=\\frac{13\\pi }{8}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
