    "q-280018": {
      "dom_id": "step-q280018",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Consider the equation $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-{4}^{∘})-1=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ If the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ are written in **ascending order**, what are their values?\n\n${x}_{1}=${{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,$\n${x}_{2}=${{field-2}}${}^{∘},\\,$\n${x}_{3}=${{field-3}}${}^{∘},\\,$\n${x}_{4}=${{field-4}}${}^{∘}$",
      "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nFirst, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-{4}^{∘})-1 & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-{4}^{∘}) & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-{4}^{∘}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{4}^{∘} & ={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}, & \\, & \\, & 2x-{4}^{∘} & ={150}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={34}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={154}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={17}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & x & ={77}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={17}^{∘}$ and $x={77}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={197}^{∘}$ and $x={257}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx={17}^{∘},{77}^{∘},{197}^{∘},{257}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={17}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={77}^{∘},\\,{x}_{3}={197}^{∘},\\,{x}_{4}={257}^{∘}\n$$",
