    "q-8376": {
      "dom_id": "step-q8376",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Consider the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+{30}^{∘})=-\\frac{1}{2}$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ If the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is the numerical value of ${x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+{30}^{∘} & =-{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}, & \\, & \\, & 2x+{30}^{∘} & ={210}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-{60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={180}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ x & =-{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & x & ={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=-{30}^{∘}$ and $x={90}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={150}^{∘}$  and $x={270}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={330}^{∘}$  and $x={450}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx={90}^{∘},{150}^{∘},{270}^{∘},{330}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${x}_{2}={150}^{∘}$ and ${x}_{3}={270}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=150\\cdot 270=40\\,500.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
