    "q-8375": {
      "dom_id": "step-q8375",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Consider the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=-\\frac{1}{2}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ If the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is ${x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi , & \\, & \\, & 2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6} & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =2n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & 2x & =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+\\frac{3n\\pi }{3} \\\\ x & =n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{(2+3n)\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\pi $ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx=0,\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\pi ,\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${x}_{2}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ and ${x}_{3}=\\pi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+\\pi =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+\\frac{3\\pi }{3}=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
