    "q-8377": {
      "dom_id": "step-q8377",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ for $0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi , & \\, & \\, & 3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & 3x & =2\\pi +2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{2n\\pi }{3} & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+\\frac{2n\\pi }{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi (4n+3)}{6} & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{2(n+1)\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ (too big)\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ (too small) and $x=0.$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ are\n\n$$\nx=0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0+\\frac{\\pi }{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
